  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 324 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nUpper ridge in place over the desert southwest with unorganized \nsurface low pressure in the northern High Plains leading to low-\nlevel warm-air advection over the central Plains. Some mid cloud \nremains but drying mid-levels brings mainly clear skies through the \nweekend with steadily warming 850 mb temperatures into at least \nearly Monday per LREF means. Continue to believe the more humid and \nslightly cooler than LREF means is on track for surface conditions \nto at least Sunday, and with temps in the mid 90s not far to the \nsouthwest Friday, a much warmer day is expected today. Confidence in \nspecifics continues to lower Monday into Tuesday with some chance \nfor upstream convection to enter the area and a generally drying \nground. This keeps the heat headlines going as-is with Warning \nconditions in much of east-central Kansas where heat indices peak \nnear/around 110 today and Sunday with slightly cooler conditions \nelsewhere and the Watch going for Monday and Tuesday though a \nboundary looks to move in around Tuesday with at least near-\nclimatological precipitation chances. In the very near term, will \nneed to monitor fog potential with light winds and a damp boundary \nlayer under clearing skies.",
